    "commit": "41784e02d46c32eef69141d09bff13260aa9d720",
    "commit_body": "Repurposes the technical_alignment (X) component as a confidence\ncoefficient gating d (trend_dominance) instead of contributing only\nadditive points. When the 5 base components (TREND, BB, RSI, MACD,\nStoch) cancel each other (the PSKY 3/20 case: TREND extreme bearish\nbut BB/RSI/MACD/Stoch bullish), x_conf collapses toward 0 and trend's\nweight contribution is gated down, restoring sideways-regime weights\nand letting the contradicting components dominate.\n\nFormula: agreement = max(bull,bear)/n; sig_str = |avg_dist|/50;\nx_conf = sig_str * agreement^2; d_eff = d * x_conf^0.5.\n\nValidated 5y diff-assess (experiments/x_conf_counter_trend.py):\nCT-PUT bucket (overall<=25, trend>=70) on 22-now: N 541->934\n(+73%), WR15 79.5%->81.9%. Same direction in every annual window.\nNaturally absorbs the counter-trend amplifier hypothesis (#11).\n\nExposes d_eff and x_conf in weight_info for explain-scores audits.",
    "commit_short": "41784e02",
    "commit_subject": "Add v22 X-confidence gate on trend dominance",
